XZ for Java — decoder subset, vendored for the Component Manager
=================================================================

Origin:   https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz-java  (tag v1.12, commit 9c58916)
Licence:  0BSD (see below) — every file keeps its SPDX header.
Package:  org.tukaani.xz → app.revanced.extension.gamehub.components.xz
          (renamed so it can never collide with a copy the host may ship later).

What is here: exactly the transitive closure of XZInputStream — the .xz
container reader, LZMA2 decoder, BCJ/delta filter decoders and the CRC/SHA
checks. No encoder, no seekable reader, no LZMAInputStream (.lzma). Nothing
else was changed besides the package name.

Why: Winlator-community .wcp components are tar archives compressed with
zstd OR xz. The host ships zstd-jni but no xz decoder (org.tukaani and
commons-compress are both absent from the 6.3.1 dex), so xz .wcp files
could not be injected without this.

Re-vendoring: fetch the tag's tarball, then
  javac -sourcepath src -d out src/org/tukaani/xz/XZInputStream.java
lists the closure as emitted .class files; copy those sources with the
package rewrite (sed 's/org\.tukaani\.xz/app.revanced.extension.gamehub.components.xz/g').

